they've been through weeks of untold  horrors in the bunkers and tunnels of  the azov style steel works in mariopol  this is the first group of evacuees to  make the perilous journey from  russian-controlled territory to the  ukrainian-controlled city of zapposia in  the red cross united nations convoy  you don't understand how terrible it was  you sit in the bomb shelter in a wet  basement and everything is shaking like  that and then when we could go up to the  surface i saw it for the second time in  a month a huge crater 15 meters wide and  who knows how deep  yes the military did share things with  us but it was the azov battalion so you  can imagine what they said we were told  that nobody needed us we felt abandoned  that we were nothing  for the past month supplies of food and  water have been severely rationed adults  going hungry for days to keep their  children fed  this is a moment of huge relief  russia said some evacuees have been  taken to a village controlled by  moscow-backed separatists and would be  allowed to travel to ukrainian held  territory if they wanted  but fears are growing for those left  behind in the confines of the steel  works  soon after the departure of the first  evacuees russian-backed forces resumed  their assault firing rockets towards the  plant  the mayor of mariopol says 200 civilians  still remain trapped inside including  several dozen small children  it's the last remaining area of the city  not under russian control  and the last refuge for hundreds of  ukrainian troops who refused to  surrender  the rest of mariopol is in ruins  but around a hundred thousand people  remain living amongst the rubble  tatiana  no longer flinches at the sound of  exploding shells  you wake up in the morning and you cry  you cry in the evening i don't know  where to go i am not alone here  imagine everything is destroyed where  should the people go now here they are  sitting with small kids  in the west of ukraine russia's launch  renewed attacks on the port city of  odessa where ukrainian officials say a  missile hit a children's dormitory  killing a 14 year old boy  missiles also struck a logistics center  used to deliver foreign weaponry  russia so far failed to land troops in  the city by sea  but seizing odessa would give russia  control of the whole of ukraine's black  sea coast  neve barker al jazeera
 

